---

Downstream Traceability

SO-F-005 and other execution-related engineering artifacts shall maintain traceability to the approved decision information upon which execution is based.

Where an authorization mechanism is established, the relationship between:

Generated Decision
        ↓
Authorization
        ↓
Approved Decision

shall also be traceable.

---

Authority Traceability

The architecture currently does not identify a finalized authority mechanism.

Therefore, no specific authority artifact is referenced as a parent or dependency at this stage.

Once the authority architecture is formally established, SO-F-004 shall be updated to maintain traceability to the applicable authority requirements, constraints, and governance mechanisms.

---

Traceability Notes

All engineering artifacts implementing adaptive decision generation shall maintain traceability to SO-F-004, either directly or through approved child objectives.

Decision-related artifacts shall preserve sufficient lineage to establish how generated decisions relate to the operating context that informed them.

Traceability shall not be used to imply authorization; a traceable generated decision remains distinct from an approved decision until the applicable authority mechanism has been satisfied.
